================================================================================
## Single "Add Data Assets" dialog for Unity Catalog import
================================================================================

Context: Importing Unity Catalog tables under Context > Data Assets went through
three stacked popups: "Select Unity Catalog Location" (a widget with a nested
"Select Catalog & Schema" picker), then a "Select Tables to Import" list, then
the import. Design was agreed in brainstorming: one dialog holds the catalog and
schema pickers, the table list and the Import action. Backend endpoints
(`/domain/metadata/list-tables`, `/domain/metadata/initialize-async`) and the
shared UCLocationWidget are unchanged; the Change Data Asset modal is unchanged.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_metadata.html
   Replaced `#tableSelectionModal` and `#loadMetadataLocationModal` with one
   `#addDataAssetsModal` (modal-xl). It holds Catalog and Schema selects, a
   "Context" shortcut button, a placeholder/spinner/list area, the permission
   banner, Select All / Deselect All / Select New Only, the filter, and the
   footer button `#importSelectedBtn` ("Add N assets"). Existing IDs and
   `data-meta-action` values are kept.
2. src/front/static/domain/js/domain-metadata.js
   - Removed `loadMetadataModal`, `loadMetadataWidgetInitialized`,
     `pendingLoadCatalog`, `pendingLoadSchema`.
   - `showLoadMetadataModal()` opens the single dialog and fills catalogs and the
     context shortcut from `UCLocationWidget.loadCatalogs()` and
     `UCLocationWidget.loadDomainLocation()`.
   - New `onAddDataAssetsCatalogChange()`, `onAddDataAssetsSchemaChange()`,
     `useContextLocationForAssets()`, `resetAddDataAssetsListing()`,
     `getAddDataAssetsLocation()`, `_showAddAssetsState()`, `_setSelectValue()`,
     `_optionHtml()`.
   - `loadMetadataFromUC()` replaced by `loadTablesForSelection(catalog, schema)`:
     lists tables inline when a schema is picked. A request-id guard drops stale
     responses. Same initial selection logic (new tables up to the import limit).
   - `showTableSelectionModal()` renamed `renderImportTable()` and no longer
     opens a modal.
   - `importSelectedTables()` reads catalog and schema from the dialog and hides
     `#addDataAssetsModal`. Fixed `const selectedTables` being reassigned on the
     import-limit path (would throw a TypeError).
   - Template bindings: `load-from-uc` removed, `add-assets-use-context` added,
     catalog and schema `change` events routed to the new handlers.
3. src/front/static/global/css/permissions.css
   Removed the `#loadMetadataConfirmBtn` read-only selector (element no longer
   exists). `#importSelectedBtn` and `[data-meta-action="show-load-modal"]` gates
   are unchanged.
4. tests/units/front/test_add_data_assets_dialog.py (new)
   Source-contract tests for the single dialog: legacy modals gone, required
   hooks present, no chained-modal state in JS, inline schema listing, import
   reads from the dialog, read-only gate.
5. tests/units/front/test_mapping_metric_view_ui.py
   Copy test retargeted from the removed `#loadMetadataConfirmBtn` to
   `#importSelectedBtn` ("Add 0 assets").
6. tests/units/front/test_data_assets_import_limit.py
   Import-limit contract now looks for `renderImportTable` (renamed from
   `showTableSelectionModal`). Limit check unchanged.
7. docs/user-guide.md
   Step 3 "Import Table Metadata" rewritten for the single dialog.
8. docs/getting-started.md
   Assign Data Assets step describes the single dialog.
9. docs/examples.md
   Step 2 "Load Data Source" updated to the single dialog.

