## Move sidebar collapse toggle into L2 left of Context

Context: The collapse/expand control lived at the top of the sidebar rail,
so it moved with the rail and competed with section links. Move it to a fixed
L2 position immediately left of the Context name (still visible on Settings,
left of the return link) so the control stays put while the rail collapses.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/base.html
   - Added fixed `#obSidebarToggle` / `#obSidebarToggleItem` as the first L2
     item (not under `data-subnav-domain-chrome`), left of the Context crumb.
2. src/front/static/global/js/sidebar-nav.js
   - Stopped injecting `.sidebar-toggle` into the rail; wire and reveal the L2
     button when a `.sidebar-nav` exists; sync `aria-pressed` / title via
     `_syncToggleChrome`.
3. src/front/static/global/css/main.css
   - Styled `.ob-subnav-sidebar-toggle` to the L2 rail height with no hover fill.
